															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/will-cloverfield" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6360865); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6360865&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605970384" alt="Will Cloverfield" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6360865)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/will-cloverfield" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(6360865); return false;" >Will Cloverfield</a></span> <span class="odate time_1605387302 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Nov 2020 20:55</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4818567">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Paranoid Fiction/Comedy (Probably)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Pitch</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Pitch&nbsp;Contents</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><br />
Basically the anomaly is the creation or knowledge of very specific theories about the meaning behind the phrase “green crab”, these theories always appear to be missing something, have experimental information or are incomplete. No one has been able to fully prove nor disprove one of these theories. These specific theories of “green crab” have the anomalous effect to always appear “interesting”.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Narrative&nbsp;Contents</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><br />
The main narrative is about how human nature can cause a once menial or previously nonexistent idea to spiral out of control due to fanaticism, or obsession. The people infected by this SCP begin to evolve, they begin to collaborate, they begin to form initiative groups or clubs to become more efficient and get people to join basically their fanbase. They start trying to get their messages out, they begin trying to recruit, convert or infect the minds of those who weren’t aware of these ideas but now are. 1-2 companies begin to catch on and take this to their advantage and begin to capitalize on the interest, making merchandise or media about such an idea as people will always be interested in the ideas and theories, the companies would always have customers. The foundation now aims to silence, disrupts collaboration, disbands many of the groups and amnestizes many of the people within the groups. But ultimately the idea will inevitably surface again even if all the groups or previous infected persons were amnesticized.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Its a cold/outsider perspective on the development of obsession and evolution of specific ideas into something much more.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Overall I need assistance with mainly containment procedures, narrative pacing/order, and writing style/tone.</p>
<p><strong>An Update Maybe</strong>:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Update</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide&nbsp;Update</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><br />
After reading suggestions I have thought of a potential update, the effect can be changed to a lesser effect instead of just making the believers obsess about it permanently I could making it more of a persuasive effect, to elaborate basically it makes it appear interesting permanently. Basically after you realize one of the theories of green crab, it appears interesting to you, you’re not compelled to do anything about it, as it’s only able to keep you anomalously interested.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

