<p>Thank you for the feedback, again sorry for my late reply.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Reply</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide&nbsp;Reply</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Yeah I can see what you mean with compulsion effect weakening it, I’ve been trying to avoid such an effect occur. (Update contents at the top may be fix for this)</p>
<p>The overall narrative I’m thinking appears to be too straight forward in this case then, as it appears so this can be an alternative</p>
<p><strong>Discovery:</strong> Small group of people effected (about 50ish) it appears to just be a self contained anomaly but growing, the people are watched over by the foundation, nothing much occurs.</p>
<p><strong>Spread:</strong> they begin to find each other and begin to cooperate to converse about their interests (just like if you found someone you had similar hobbies with) This is when the groups begin to form. The group is in phase beta (just development and all).</p>
<p>At the same time others around the world also begin to have this anomalous phenomenon occur to them, it appears it wasn’t self contained.</p>
<p><strong>Culture spread:</strong> Websites, Social Media, Clubs, flyers about the green crab are made for the individuals to be connected further. (I’ll elaborate on the specifics in the future if this is good) The foundation steps in and makes this harder.</p>
<p>This is the alpha phase of the groups as they are more developed and now want to invite others to join them like how regular people look for others.</p>
<p>It appears the anomaly has become a hobby or idol to those interested (just like video games or celebrities regular people are interested</p>
<p><strong>Popular culture takeover:</strong><br />
As the theories spread throughout media via the instances, it integrates itself as minor pop culture at first, as it always appears as interesting why would you need any other type of media to satisfy audiences? Some companies would begin to create fiction about the green crab adding more theories to the pot. If unregulated these theories of this SCP would eventually overshadow other works of media. This would eventually become the only piece of entertainment we’d want.</p>
<p>What groups form: Currently still deciding group names, but I’m probably going to make it a general community kind of like how we have communities for specific games etc, they may have different beliefs but they’re all part of the “green crab” community or whatever I decide to name them. And just like regular communities groups will probably have different names and qualities to themselves.</p>
<p>Church Group<br />
Hobbyist Group<br />
Scientific Group<br />
Conspiracist Group<br />
Philosophical Group</p>
<p>What happens to the groups: basically a change in terms of their ambition, influence on media and pop culture, as their ideas become more mainstream (as mainstream as a foundation watched anomaly could be) so does the size of their groups.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

